#' Trust and stress in three countries (simulated)
#'
#' Simulated survey data used in the examples and tests. Two correlated
#' factors, trust and stress, are each measured by four 5-point Likert items
#' in three countries. Loadings are equal in all countries, but item `stress3`
#' has a shifted intercept in Brazil, so loading invariance holds and
#' intercept invariance does not. Twelve values per item are missing at random.
#' The data are generated by `tools/make_examples.R`.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 1200 rows and 9 variables:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{country}{Factor: Chile (n = 420), Brazil (n = 380), Spain (n = 400).}
#'   \item{trust1, trust2, trust3, trust4}{Ordered factors with levels 1 to 5.}
#'   \item{stress1, stress2, stress3, stress4}{Ordered factors with levels 1 to 5.}
#' }
"wizdata"
